---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import LegalIdentity from '../../components/LegalIdentity.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, LEGAL, SITE_NAMES, SITE_URL } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
const lang = 'en';
const updated = '2026-10-09';
---
<PageLayout title={`Privacy policy – ${SITE_NAMES[lang]}`} description="Data handled by CalculAides: no inputs sent, no cookie, anonymous cookie-free stability monitoring by Microsoft Clarity; only the host’s technical logs. Your rights under the GDPR and how to contact the CNIL." lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Privacy' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p>This page describes the processing of personal data linked to {SITE_URL}, under articles 12 to 14 of Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (GDPR) and the French Data Protection Act of 6 January 1978.</p>
    <h2>1. Controller</h2>
    <LegalIdentity lang={lang} />
    <p>Contact: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. No data protection officer has been appointed, as the conditions of article 37 GDPR are not met.</p>
    <h2>2. Your inputs stay in your browser</h2>
    <p>Rent, income, household, number of children, disability: whatever you type into a calculator is processed by your own browser and <strong>is sent to no server</strong>, stored nowhere and tied to no identifier. Such details can be sensitive, which is why no audience measurement tool is loaded. The share link puts your inputs in the page address: give it only to people you choose.</p>
    <h2>3. Processing carried out</h2>
    <h3>Host connection logs</h3><p>The host records IP address, date, page requested, browser and referring page. Purpose: security and diagnosis. Legal basis: legitimate interest (art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). Retention: under the host’s own policy (GitHub).</p>
    <h3>No cookie, no analytics</h3><p>The site sets no cookie, uses no browser storage and loads no audience statistics, advertising or social media tool. There is therefore no consent banner: there is nothing to accept.</p><h3>Anonymous stability monitoring (Microsoft Clarity, cookie-free)</h3><p>To catch script errors, slow pages and buttons that do not respond, the site loads Microsoft Clarity in its cookie-free mode: no Clarity cookie (<code>_clck</code>, <code>_clsk</code>, <code>MUID</code>, <code>CLID</code>) is set, each page view gets a one-off identifier, and page content and your inputs are masked. Controller: Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited. Purpose: stability and technical quality of the site. Retention: 30 days for recordings, 13 months for aggregate statistics. Legal basis: legitimate interest (art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). To object: block clarity.ms in your browser (the calculators keep working) or write to the address below.</p>
    <h3>Messages you send</h3><p>If you write to the contact address, your message is kept while we answer and fix any error, then deleted within twelve months.</p>
    <h2>4. Recipients</h2><p>No data is sold or passed on. The host, GitHub, acts as a processor under article 28 GDPR; Microsoft receives the masked, cookie-free stability data described above.</p>
    <h2>5. Transfers outside the EU</h2><p>GitHub, Inc. is based in the United States; connection logs may be processed there under the EU–U.S. Data Privacy Framework and the European Commission’s standard contractual clauses.</p>
    <h2>6. Your rights</h2><p>Rights of access, rectification, erasure, restriction, objection and portability (articles 15 to 22 GDPR): write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>, answer within one month. You may complain to the {LEGAL.supervisoryAuthority}: <a href={LEGAL.supervisoryAuthorityUrl} rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">{LEGAL.supervisoryAuthorityUrl}</a>.</p>
    <h2>7. No automated decision</h2><p>A calculator result is an estimate produced at your request, with no legal effect: it is not a decision within article 22 GDPR and does not bind the CAF.</p>
    <p>See also the <a href={route('cookies', lang)}>cookies</a> page. Last updated: {updated}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
